along the edges."},"defenceVal":"2","mp":"340","price":"1200","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1026005","name":{"zh":"束发","en":"Hair Tie"},"level":"0","description":{"zh":"用来束起长发的简单布条，简单有效。","en":"A simple cloth strip for tying up long hair. Simple and effective."},"mp":"100","price":"200","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"children":{"label":{"zh":"子女","en":"Children"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10786","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI103615","name":{"zh":"陈郡何氏","en":"The He clan of Chen"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自姬姓，战国韩厘王之后。韩国灭后子孙散居陈郡，以何为氏。东汉何熙官至车骑将军。何夔为曹魏太仆、太子太傅，封成阳亭侯。其子何曾为西晋太宰，封朗陵公。何劭、何绥皆显于西晋，绵延近两百年。","en":"Originating from the Ji surname, descendants of King Xi of Han during the Warring States period. After the fall of the Han state, descendants scattered across Chen Commandery and adopted He as their surname. In the Eastern Han, He Xi rose to General of Chariots and Cavalry. He Kui served Cao Wei as Minister of the Coach and Grand Tutor to the Crown Prince, enfeoffed as Marquis of Chengyang Pavilion. His son He Zeng served Western Jin as Grand Chancellor, enfeoffed as Duke of Langling. He Shao and He Sui both attained prominent positions in Western Jin, maintaining the clan's prominence for nearly two hundred years."},"talent":{"military":"1","commerce":"6","politics":"7"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"何夔","height":"较矮","shape":"一般"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1045","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"0","role":0,"stats":[45,30,80,78,82,85],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"0","reputation":"3200","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007002","armor":"WP1014105","helmet":"WP1026005"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"zh":"汉末三杰","en":"Three Heroes of the Late Han"},"year":"